    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n66995" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετάτροπ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>turning about,
			returning</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. ἐκ βυθοῦ ἔρρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.506.5
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Del.</u>
				99
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. αὖραι</span>
			<i>veering</i> winds, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>El.</u>
				1147
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολέμον μ. αὔρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pax</u>
					945
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>turning round upon</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαίμων μ. ἐπί τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					943
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετάτροπα ἔργα</span>
			deeds <i>that turn upon their author</i> or <i>are visited with
				vengeance</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				89
			</span></i>.</div>
